DZVP-MOLOPT-GTH: transcribed from CP2K's BASIS_MOLOPT by scripts/cp2k2bsd (H C N O)
PP-PROVENANCE H=1 C=4 N=5 O=6
Coefficients as CP2K states them (normalized primitives); one shell per CP2K contraction, the set's exponents shared.
CP2K runs every basis SPHERICAL: compare against it with basis.spherical true.
GATE (2026-11-02, H C N O): 15 bohr box, Gamma, GTH-PADE q1/q4/q5/q6, spherical, Becke (60, GL 48), solid.densityEcut 100 Ha,
vs CP2K 1200 Ry: CH4 -8.0351300 vs -8.0351296 (-0.4 uHa), NH3 -11.7016472 vs -11.7016477 (+0.5), H2O -17.1824850 vs -17.1824875
(+2.5).  STATE densityEcut: the AUTO value (2 alpha_max = 24 Ha) truncates the density's G-ball on the sharp O/N pairs --
CH4 11, NH3 66, H2O 330 uHa high (OpenWork density-ball row).  Run it on a stated Becke mesh: the default (40, 29) is 52 uHa
short on CH4.
BENZENE (2026-11-03, 18 bohr box, same recipe): -37.6867871 vs CP2K -37.6867742 (-13.0 uHa, 1.1 uHa/atom; Exc -9.4 of it).

